# Everything the image does not need, and two things it must never receive.
#
# `.env` and `.env.local` are the two: they hold real API keys, and a build
# context that carries them bakes them into a layer that anyone who can pull
# the image can read. Fly secrets are injected at runtime (§6.2); nothing in
# the image should ever contain a value.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Tests and fixtures. The image runs the app; CI runs the tests, against a
# checkout, with a database. Shipping them costs size and widens what a
# compromised container can read.
tests/
docker-compose*.yml

.git/
.github/
*.md
!README.md
